WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.269
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Sarah. Welcome to Online Proficiency.

2
00:00:05.569 --> 00:00:08.630
Hi! I'm Rithy. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:16.134
Unit twenty-nine: Philosophy of Education. In this unit, you will debate what education is truly for.

4
00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.581
Socratic method.

5
00:00:19.281 --> 00:00:25.471
Socratic method means teaching through questions that make learners examine their own ideas.

6
00:00:25.771 --> 00:00:29.083
The Socratic method turns a lecture into a conversation.

7
00:00:29.783 --> 00:00:32.691
Your turn. Say: Socratic method.

8
00:00:35.391 --> 00:00:36.624
Socratic method.

9
00:00:37.617 --> 00:00:39.198
liberal education.

10
00:00:39.898 --> 00:00:45.926
liberal education means a broad education in arts and sciences that develops the whole mind.

11
00:00:46.226 --> 00:00:50.362
A liberal education teaches you how to think, not what to think.

12
00:00:51.062 --> 00:00:54.342
Your turn. Say: liberal education.

13
00:00:57.042 --> 00:00:58.495
liberal education.

14
00:00:59.483 --> 00:01:01.402
emancipatory education.

15
00:01:02.102 --> 00:01:08.153
emancipatory education means education that aims to free people from oppression and dependence.

16
00:01:08.453 --> 00:01:13.994
Emancipatory education helped farmers read their own land contracts.

17
00:01:14.694 --> 00:01:18.391
Your turn. Say: emancipatory education.

18
00:01:21.091 --> 00:01:23.079
emancipatory education.

19
00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:25.874
pedagogy of the oppressed.

20
00:01:26.574 --> 00:01:33.914
pedagogy of the oppressed means Paulo Freire's theory that education should empower the poor to change society.

21
00:01:34.214 --> 00:01:38.036
Pedagogy of the oppressed begins with the learners' own lives.

22
00:01:38.736 --> 00:01:42.468
Your turn. Say: pedagogy of the oppressed.

23
00:01:45.168 --> 00:01:46.854
pedagogy of the oppressed.

24
00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:49.873
banking model of education.

25
00:01:50.573 --> 00:01:56.682
banking model of education means Freire's term for teachers 'depositing' facts into passive students.

26
00:01:56.982 --> 00:02:01.199
Copying from the board all day is the banking model of education.

27
00:02:01.899 --> 00:02:05.852
Your turn. Say: banking model of education.

28
00:02:08.552 --> 00:02:10.389
banking model of education.

29
00:02:11.383 --> 00:02:12.175
Bildung.

30
00:02:12.875 --> 00:02:17.975
Bildung means the German ideal of education as lifelong self-cultivation.

31
00:02:18.275 --> 00:02:21.505
For Humboldt, Bildung meant shaping one's whole character.

32
00:02:22.205 --> 00:02:24.799
Your turn. Say: Bildung.

33
00:02:27.499 --> 00:02:28.350
Bildung.

34
00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:30.874
character education.

35
00:02:31.574 --> 00:02:37.869
character education means teaching values such as honesty, respect and responsibility.

36
00:02:38.169 --> 00:02:41.991
Character education is part of every C2-EPE lesson.

37
00:02:42.691 --> 00:02:46.052
Your turn. Say: character education.

38
00:02:48.752 --> 00:02:50.136
character education.

39
00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:52.778
critical consciousness.

40
00:02:53.478 --> 00:02:59.413
critical consciousness means the ability to recognise and question social and political injustice.

41
00:02:59.713 --> 00:03:03.559
Literacy classes awakened critical consciousness among workers.

42
00:03:04.259 --> 00:03:07.724
Your turn. Say: critical consciousness.

43
00:03:10.424 --> 00:03:11.924
critical consciousness.

44
00:03:12.917 --> 00:03:14.963
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:03:15.263 --> 00:03:19.015
Ms. Sarah, is school just about passing exams?

46
00:03:20.317 --> 00:03:26.220
If it is, we are barking up the wrong tree. Education should light a fire, not fill a bucket.

47
00:03:27.517 --> 00:03:33.266
But my old school was pure banking model of education: we copied, memorised, repeated.

48
00:03:34.550 --> 00:03:39.092
Freire would say the teacher held all the cards and the students were empty vaults.

49
00:03:40.383 --> 00:03:42.406
So what is the alternative?

50
00:03:43.717 --> 00:03:48.027
The Socratic method, for one: questions that make you think on your feet.

51
00:03:49.317 --> 00:03:53.234
And character education? Isn't that just icing on the cake?

52
00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:58.387
Far from it. Knowledge without character is a ship without a rudder.

53
00:03:59.683 --> 00:04:04.237
Grammar focus: Idioms and figurative language (extended).

54
00:04:04.537 --> 00:04:07.082
Idioms and metaphors make arguments vivid.

55
00:04:07.382 --> 00:04:14.806
If school is only about exams, we are barking up the wrong tree. Education should light a fire, not fill a bucket.

56
00:04:15.106 --> 00:04:18.360
Knowledge without character is a ship without a rudder.

57
00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:27.242
At C2, use figurative language sparingly and precisely: one vivid image persuades more than five clichés.

58
00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:31.390
Now read and listen. What Is Education For?.

59
00:04:31.690 --> 00:04:37.312
Philosophers have argued about the purpose of education for more than two thousand years.

60
00:04:38.617 --> 00:04:43.646
Socrates taught by questioning, a practice now known as the Socratic method.

61
00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:52.232
In nineteenth-century Germany, the ideal of Bildung described education as lifelong self-cultivation.

62
00:04:53.517 --> 00:05:00.543
A liberal education, in a similar spirit, aims to develop the whole mind rather than train a single skill.

63
00:05:01.850 --> 00:05:08.343
In 1968, the Brazilian educator Paulo Freire wrote Pedagogy of the Oppressed.

64
00:05:09.650 --> 00:05:16.619
He criticised the banking model of education, in which teachers simply deposit facts into passive students.

65
00:05:17.917 --> 00:05:23.353
Instead, he called for emancipatory education that builds critical consciousness.

66
00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:31.979
Today, many schools combine these ideas with character education, hoping to produce people who are both wise and good.

67
00:05:33.283 --> 00:05:36.063
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

68
00:05:36.363 --> 00:05:40.383
Teachers 'depositing' facts into passive students is the blank.

69
00:05:40.683 --> 00:05:46.461
A, banking model of education. B, Socratic method. C, Bildung.

70
00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:54.133
The answer is A: banking model of education.

71
00:05:55.617 --> 00:05:58.150
'You're barking up the wrong tree' means you are blank.

72
00:05:58.450 --> 00:06:04.066
A, looking in the wrong place. B, shouting too loudly. C, climbing too high.

73
00:06:08.050 --> 00:06:11.060
The answer is A: looking in the wrong place.

74
00:06:12.550 --> 00:06:14.805
Teaching through questions is the blank.

75
00:06:15.105 --> 00:06:21.626
A, Socratic method. B, liberal education. C, character education.

76
00:06:25.617 --> 00:06:28.313
The answer is A: Socratic method.

77
00:06:29.817 --> 00:06:32.559
'Icing on the cake' describes something that is blank.

78
00:06:32.859 --> 00:06:38.591
A, essential. B, a pleasant extra. C, a mistake.

79
00:06:42.583 --> 00:06:45.338
The answer is B: a pleasant extra.

80
00:06:46.850 --> 00:06:50.614
According to the text, who wrote Pedagogy of the Oppressed?

81
00:06:50.914 --> 00:06:55.160
A, Paulo Freire. B, Socrates. C, Humboldt.

82
00:06:59.150 --> 00:07:01.823
The answer is A: Paulo Freire.

83
00:07:03.317 --> 00:07:10.009
Now it's your turn. Part one: What should be the main purpose of education in Cambodia today?

84
00:07:15.309 --> 00:07:21.465
Part two: Use one idiom and one metaphor; compare two models of education.

85
00:07:27.765 --> 00:07:40.437
If we only train students for exams, we are barking up the wrong tree. Education should light a fire: it should build critical consciousness and good character, not just fill a bucket with facts.

86
00:07:40.737 --> 00:07:43.259
That is a well-argued answer!

87
00:07:44.250 --> 00:07:50.049
Great work today! You learned eight new words and idioms and figurative language (extended).

88
00:07:50.349 --> 00:07:53.872
Today's value is pride in learning. Be proud of what you learned.

89
00:07:54.172 --> 00:07:56.824
See you in Unit thirty. Goodbye!

90
00:07:57.124 --> 00:07:59.823
Thank you, Ms. Sarah! Bye, everyone!

